<% content_for :title, "On Medications | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="bipolar-medications-page">

  <style>
    .bipolar-medications-page {
      --bm-black: #080808;
      --bm-white: #fff;
      --bm-pink: #ff1493;
      --bm-yellow: #eaff00;
      --bm-purple: #8a00ff;
      background: var(--bm-black);
      color: var(--bm-white);
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .bipolar-medications-page * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    .bm-hero {
      min-height: 82vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 100px 7vw;
      background-image:
        linear-gradient(
          90deg,
          rgba(8, 8, 8, .96) 0%,
          rgba(8, 8, 8, .72) 48%,
          rgba(8, 8, 8, .12) 100%
        ),
        var(--bm-desktop);
      background-position: center, right center;
      background-size: cover, cover;
    }

    .bm-hero-content {
      max-width: 1000px;
    }

    .bm-eyebrow,
    .bm-section-label,
    .bm-card-label {
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: .16em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bm-eyebrow {
      color: var(--bm-pink);
    }

    .bm-hero h1 {
      margin: 24px 0;
      font-size: clamp(58px, 10vw, 142px);
      line-height: .88;
      letter-spacing: -.07em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bm-hero h1 span {
      display: block;
    }

    .bm-intro {
      color: var(--bm-yellow);
      font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 25px);
      font-weight: 900;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .bm-section {
      padding: 76px 7vw;
      border-top: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .2);
    }

    .bm-section-inner {
      max-width: 1250px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .bm-section-label {
      color: var(--bm-pink);
    }

    .bm-section h2 {
      max-width: 850px;
      margin: 18px 0 30px;
      font-size: clamp(38px, 6vw, 78px);
      line-height: .98;
      letter-spacing: -.055em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bm-copy {
      max-width: 850px;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .bm-copy p {
      margin: 0 0 22px;
    }

    .bm-box-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 18px;
      margin-top: 34px;
    }

    .bm-box {
      padding: 24px;
      border: 2px solid var(--bm-pink);
      background: #111;
    }

    .bm-box:nth-child(2) {
      border-color: var(--bm-yellow);
    }

    .bm-box:nth-child(3) {
      border-color: var(--bm-purple);
    }

    .bm-box:nth-child(4) {
      border-color: var(--bm-white);
    }

    .bm-box h3 {
      margin: 12px 0;
      font-size: 24px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bm-box p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .bm-callout {
      max-width: 950px;
      margin: 35px 0;
      padding: 24px;
      border: 3px solid var(--bm-yellow);
      color: var(--bm-yellow);
      font-size: clamp(21px, 3vw, 34px);
      font-weight: 900;
      line-height: 1.2;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bm-ending {
      padding: 80px 7vw;
      background: var(--bm-purple);
    }

    .bm-ending-inner {
      max-width: 1250px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .bm-ending h2 {
      margin: 12px 0 24px;
      font-size: clamp(46px, 8vw, 110px);
      line-height: .92;
      letter-spacing: -.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .bm-ending p {
      max-width: 780px;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .bm-back {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 24px;
      padding: 14px 18px;
      border: 2px solid var(--bm-yellow);
      color: var(--bm-yellow);
      font-weight: 900;
      text-decoration: none;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .bm-hero {
        min-height: 75vh;
        padding: 90px 22px;
        background-image:
          linear-gradient(
            180deg,
            rgba(8, 8, 8, .55),
            rgba(8, 8, 8, .08)
          ),
          var(--bm-mobile);
        background-position: center, center bottom;
      }

      .bm-section {
        padding: 58px 22px;
      }

      .bm-box-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .bm-ending {
        padding: 65px 22px;
      }
    }
  </style>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="bm-hero"
           style="--bm-desktop: url('<%= asset_path('bipolar_medications_desktop.png') %>');
                  --bm-mobile: url('<%= asset_path('bipolar_medications_mobile.png') %>');">

    <div class="bm-hero-content">

      <p class="bm-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / ON MEDICATIONS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>ON</span>
        <span>MEDICATIONS.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="bm-intro">
        PART OF THE WORK.<br>
        NOT THE WHOLE STORY.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / YOUR ROUTINE -->
  <section class="bm-section">
    <div class="bm-section-inner">

      <p class="bm-section-label">01 / YOUR ROUTINE</p>

      <h2>
        TAKING THEM<br>
        ISN'T THE HARD PART.
      </h2>

      <div class="bm-copy">
        <p>
          You take your medication. You don’t have to invent a struggle
          with it just because medication is a complicated subject for
          some people. This is one part of your life with bipolar disorder
          that you can describe plainly: you take your meds.
        </p>

        <p>
          That routine matters to you, but it doesn’t have to become your
          whole identity or the only measure of how well you’re doing.
          Taking medication doesn’t mean every symptom disappears, and
          having a difficult episode doesn’t erase the fact that you’ve
          kept taking it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bm-callout">
        YOU CAN TAKE YOUR MEDS AND STILL NEED SUPPORT.
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / THE WHOLE PICTURE -->
  <section class="bm-section">
    <div class="bm-section-inner">

      <p class="bm-section-label">02 / THE WHOLE PICTURE</p>

      <h2>
        MEDICATION<br>
        IS ONE PART.
      </h2>

      <div class="bm-copy">
        <p>
          Living with bipolar disorder still asks things of you: noticing
          mood changes, managing impulsivity, dealing with the effects of
          depression, asking for help, and taking responsibility for
          decisions and their consequences.
        </p>

        <p>
          You’ve described overspending and impulsive decisions as real
          challenges. Those deserve attention in their own right. You
          don’t need to turn them into proof that you aren’t trying or
          that your medication routine doesn’t count.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bm-box-grid">

        <article class="bm-box">
          <p class="bm-card-label">YOU CAN</p>
          <h3>KEEP TAKING THEM</h3>
          <p>
            Medication can be part of the structure you use to care
            for yourself.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bm-box">
          <p class="bm-card-label">AND</p>
          <h3>KEEP PAYING ATTENTION</h3>
          <p>
            Your moods, sleep, energy, and choices still deserve honest
            attention.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bm-box">
          <p class="bm-card-label">AND</p>
          <h3>ASK FOR SUPPORT</h3>
          <p>
            You can bring concerns or changes to your treatment team
            without needing to prove that things are bad enough first.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bm-box">
          <p class="bm-card-label">AND</p>
          <h3>OWN YOUR CHOICES</h3>
          <p>
            Treatment and accountability can sit beside each other.
            Neither one cancels the other out.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / WHEN SOMETHING CHANGES -->
  <section class="bm-section">
    <div class="bm-section-inner">

      <p class="bm-section-label">03 / WHEN SOMETHING CHANGES</p>

      <h2>
        BRING IT<br>
        INTO THE ROOM.
      </h2>

      <div class="bm-copy">
        <p>
          If your symptoms, routine, or concerns change, you can tell your
          prescriber directly. You don’t have to make the conversation
          dramatic or show up with a perfect explanation. “Something feels
          different” is a useful place to start.
        </p>

        <p>
          Questions about your medication plan belong in a conversation
          with your health care provider. You don’t have to make changes
          to that plan on your own.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bm-callout">
        HONEST INFORMATION HELPS YOUR CARE TEAM UNDERSTAND WHAT’S HAPPENING.
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="bm-ending">
    <div class="bm-ending-inner">

      <p class="bm-section-label">KEEP THE WHOLE PERSON IN VIEW</p>

      <h2>
        TREATMENT<br>
        IS PART OF<br>
        YOUR LIFE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        You take your medication. You also have a life, responsibilities,
        relationships, symptoms, plans, and difficult days. Let the routine
        support you without reducing you to a diagnosis or a pill organizer.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO BIPOLAR",
          bipolar_path,
          class: "bm-back" %>

    </div>
  </section>

</main>